          "html": "<div class=\"cm-content-canvas\"><div class=\"cm-content-bg\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"cm-content-orb cm-content-orb--1\"></span><span class=\"cm-content-orb cm-content-orb--2\"></span><span class=\"cm-content-grid\"></span></div><div class=\"cm-content-inner\"><span class=\"cm-content-kicker\">Lesson outline</span><p class=\"cm-content-unit\">Unit 1 · 1.1</p><h2 class=\"cm-content-title\">Can change occur at an instant?</h2><p class=\"cm-content-lede\">5 sections · theory, examples, and AP-style checks.</p><ol class=\"cm-content-list\"><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"cm-content-item\" data-cm-jump-section=\"4\"><span class=\"cm-content-num\">01</span><span class=\"cm-content-copy\"><strong>Average vs instantaneous</strong><span>Jump to section</span></span><span class=\"cm-content-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></button></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"cm-content-item\" data-cm-jump-section=\"7\"><span class=\"cm-content-num\">02</span><span class=\"cm-content-copy\"><strong>Secant slopes</strong><span>Jump to section</span></span><span class=\"cm-content-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></button></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"cm-content-item\" data-cm-jump-section=\"10\"><span class=\"cm-content-num\">03</span><span class=\"cm-content-copy\"><strong>Graph interpretation</strong><span>Jump to section</span></span><span class=\"cm-content-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></button></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"cm-content-item\" data-cm-jump-section=\"12\"><span class=\"cm-content-num\">04</span><span class=\"cm-content-copy\"><strong>AP-style MCQ</strong><span>Jump to section</span></span><span class=\"cm-content-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></button></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"cm-content-item\" data-cm-jump-section=\"14\"><span class=\"cm-content-num\">05</span><span class=\"cm-content-copy\"><strong>Practice packet</strong><span>Jump to section</span></span><span class=\"cm-content-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></button></li></ol></div></div>",
          "kind": "content",
          "group": "divider",
          "section": "1.1",
          "study_tip": ""
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "title": "Section 01 · Average vs instantaneous",
          "html": "<div class=\"cm-section-divider\"><span class=\"cm-section-num\">01</span><span class=\"cm-section-kicker\">Up next</span><h3 class=\"cm-section-title\">Average vs instantaneous</h3></div>",
          "kind": "section",
          "group": "divider",
          "section": "1.1",
          "study_tip": ""
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "title": "The big question of calculus",
          "html": "<div class=\"cm-slide-role cm-slide-role--lesson\"><span class=\"cm-slide-role-label\">Knowledge Point</span><strong>Build the method</strong><p>Average rate uses an interval; instantaneous rate asks about a single instant.</p></div><p>Calculus begins with a precise question:</p><blockquote class=\"ap-calc-quote\"><em>How can we describe what is happening at an instant when change usually takes time?</em></blockquote><p><strong>Average rate of change</strong> on \\([a,b]\\):</p><div class=\"stem-math-block cm-math-block\">\\[\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a}\\]</div><p><strong>Instantaneous rate</strong> at \\(t=a\\) uses shorter intervals and a <strong>limit</strong>.</p>",
          "kind": "lesson",
          "group": "learn",
          "section": "1.1",
          "study_tip": ""
        },
        {
          "index": 5,
          "title": "Secant slopes shrink toward a tangent",
          "html": "<div class=\"cm-slide-role cm-slide-role--lesson\"><span class=\"cm-slide-role-label\">Knowledge Point</span><strong>Build the method</strong><p>Shrink the interval — the secant slope approaches the tangent slope.</p></div><p>For position \\(s(t)=t^2+1\\), the average rate from \\(t=2\\) to \\(t=2+h\\) is</p><div class=\"stem-math-block cm-math-block\">\\[\\frac{s(2+h)-s(2)}{h}=4+h\\]</div><p>As \\(h\\to 0\\), the rate approaches <strong>\\(4\\)</strong>. That limiting value is the instantaneous rate at \\(t=2\\).</p>",
          "kind": "lesson",
          "group": "learn",
          "section": "1.1",
          "study_tip": ""
        },
        {
          "index": 6,
          "title": "Section 02 · Secant → tangent",
          "html": "<div class=\"cm-section-divider\"><span class=\"cm-section-num\">02</span><span class=\"cm-section-kicker\">Up next</span><h3 class=\"cm-section-title\">Secant → tangent</h3></div>",
          "kind": "section",
          "group": "divider",
          "section": "1.1",
          "study_tip": ""
        },
        {
          "index": 7,
          "title": "Worked example: simplify the difference quotient",
          "html": "<div class=\"cm-slide-role cm-slide-role--lesson\"><span class=\"cm-slide-role-label\">Worked Example</span><strong>Show every algebra step</strong><p>Expand, cancel \\(h\\), then interpret the limit.</p></div><p>Given \\(s(t)=t^2+1\\), simplify \\(\\dfrac{s(2+h)-s(2)}{h}\\).</p><div class=\"stem-math-block cm-math-block\">\\[\\frac{(2+h)^2+1-(4+1)}{h}=\\frac{4h+h^2}{h}=4+h\\]</div><p>So the instantaneous rate at \\(t=2\\) is <strong>\\(4\\)</strong>.</p>",
          "kind": "lesson",
          "group": "learn",
          "section": "1.1",
          "study_tip": ""
        },
        {
          "index": 8,
          "title": "Section 03 · Context graphs",
          "html": "<div class=\"cm-section-divider\"><span class=\"cm-section-num\">03</span><span class=\"cm-section-kicker\">Up next</span><h3 class=\"cm-section-title\">Context graphs</h3></div>",
          "kind": "section",
          "group": "divider",
          "section": "1.1",
          "study_tip": ""
        },
        {
          "index": 9,
          "title": "Interpreting motion on a graph (packet: Mr. Brust)",
          "html": "<div class=\"cm-slide-role cm-slide-role--lesson\"><span class=\"cm-slide-role-label\">Application</span><strong>Read the graph</strong><p>Slope of a secant = average rate; tangent slope ≈ instantaneous rate.</p></div><p>Distance-from-home \\(D(t)\\) vs. time: turning around creates a non-monotonic graph.</p><ul class=\"stem-itemize\"><li><strong>(a)</strong> Average speed for the whole trip: \\(\\dfrac{D(8)-D(0)}{8-0}\\).</li><li><strong>(b)</strong> Average rate from \\(t=2\\) to \\(t=6\\): slope of the secant on that interval.</li><li><strong>(c)</strong> Near \\(t=2\\), use a <em>short</em> interval (e.g. \\(2\\) to \\(2.1\\)) to estimate the instantaneous rate.</li></ul>",
          "kind": "lesson",
          "group": "learn",
          "section": "1.1",
          "study_tip": ""
        },
        {
          "index": 10,
          "title": "Social-media views: tangent at w = 10",
          "html": "<div class=\"cm-slide-role cm-slide-role--lesson\"><span class=\"cm-slide-role-label\">Application</span><strong>Estimate from the graph</strong><p>Draw a tangent line; its slope estimates the instantaneous rate.</p></div><p>Channel views \\(v(w)\\) vs. weeks \\(w\\): at \\(w=10\\), sketch a tangent line and estimate its slope (views per week at that instant).</p><p>To <em>estimate</em> without a tangent, use average rate on a tiny interval: \\(\\dfrac{v(10.1)-v(9.9)}{0.2}\\).</p>",
          "kind": "lesson",
          "group": "learn",
          "section": "1.1",
          "study_tip": ""
        },
        {
          "index": 11,
          "title": "Section 04 · AP-style MCQ",
          "html": "<div class=\"cm-section-divider\"><span class=\"cm-section-num\">04</span><span class=\"cm-section-kicker\">Up next</span><h3 class=\"cm-section-title\">AP-style MCQ</h3></div>",
          "kind": "section",
          "group": "divider",
