        },
        {
          "index": 12,
          "title": "Answer: limit interpretation",
          "html": "<div class=\"cm-slide-role cm-slide-role--answer\"><span class=\"cm-slide-role-label\">Answer Review</span><strong>Check and correct</strong><p>Compare your work with the final answer and fix any missed step.</p></div><p><strong>Correct Answer: C</strong></p><div class=\"cm-try-banner\" data-cm-try-banner><div class=\"cm-try-banner-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\">✦</div><div class=\"cm-try-banner-copy\"><strong>Your turn</strong><span>Work it out on paper first — reveal when you're ready.</span></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"cm-reveal-btn\" data-cm-reveal-solution>Show solution</button></div><p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><div class=\"cm-solution-panel cm-is-collapsed\" data-cm-solution-panel><p>A limit statement is always about <strong>approaching</strong> inputs and outputs — choice C.</p></div>",
